! Lab 09: ACLs and Network Security
! Platform: Cisco Packet Tracer
! Devices: R1, ISP, SW1, SW2
! Purpose:
! - Understand basic network security with ACLs
! - Configure standard and extended ACLs
! - Control traffic between networks
! - Restrict access to internal VLANs
! - Understand permit and deny logic
! - Verify ACL behaviour with ping tests
! - Apply ACLs to router interfaces


! Verify ACL configuration
show access-lists

! Important output:
! access-list 100 deny ip 198.51.100.0 0.0.0.255 192.168.0.0 0.0.255.255
! access-list 100 permit ip any any

! Verify interface ACL assignment
show running-config interface gigabitEthernet 0/1

! Important output:
! ip access-group 100 in

! Verify security behaviour

! From Internet-PC:
ping 192.168.10.10
ping 192.168.20.10

! Result:
! failed replies
! ACL successfully blocked inbound Internet access to internal VLANs

! From Sales-PC1:
ping 198.51.100.10

! Result:
! successful replies

! Internal VLAN users can still reach outward networks

! Save configuration
write memory